{"ref":"BDB, סָגָן","hw":"סָגָן","html":"† <big>[<span dir=\"rtl\">סָגָן</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">סֶ֫גֶן</span>]</big>  <strong>n.m. prefect, ruler (</strong>loan-word from Assyrian <em>šaknu</em>, <em>prefect</em> of conquered city or province (√ <em>šakânu</em>, <em>set, appoint</em>) Dl<sup>HWB 659</sup>, cf. Schr<sup>COT</sup> <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 41:25\" href=\"/Isaiah.41.25\">Is 41:25</a>; appar. = NH <span dir=\"rtl\">סָגָן</span>, <span dir=\"rtl\">סֶגֶן</span>, Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">סִגְנָא</span> <em>a superior</em> (not <em>high</em>) <em>priest;</em> Mand. <span dir=\"rtl\">אשגאנדא</span> WBrandt<sup>Mand. Schriften 169</sup> <em>a candidate for priesthood;</em> cf. Jen in Brandt<sup>ib.</sup>; hence perhaps Gk. ζωγάνης, cf. Lewy<sup>Fremdw. 129</sup><strong>)</strong>;—only pl. <span dir=\"rtl\">סְגָנִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.6\">Ez 23:6</a> + 14 times; sf. <span dir=\"rtl\">סְגָנֶיהָ</span> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:57\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.57\">Je 51:57</a> + v <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:58\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.58\">58</a> (where read prob. <span dir=\"rtl\">סְגָנָיו</span> 𝔊 Gie);—<br><strong>1.</strong>  <em>prefects</em> of Assyr. and Bab. <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:6\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.6\">Ez 23:6</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:12\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.12\">12</a>, <a data-ref=\"Ezekiel 23:23\" href=\"/Ezekiel.23.23\">23</a> <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:23\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.23\">Je 51:23</a>, <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:57\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.57\">57</a> (all + <span dir=\"rtl\">פַּחוֹת</span>), <a data-ref=\"Isaiah 41:25\" href=\"/Isaiah.41.25\">Is 41:25</a>, of king of Medes <a data-ref=\"Jeremiah 51:28\" href=\"/Jeremiah.51.28\">Je 51:28</a> (+ <span dir=\"rtl\">פַּחוֹת</span>).<br><strong>2.</strong>  <em>petty rulers, officials</em> of Judah (only Ne Ezr in sources): disting. from <span dir=\"rtl\">חֹרִים</span> <em>nobles</em> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 2:16\" href=\"/Nehemiah.2.16\">Ne 2:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 4:8\" href=\"/Nehemiah.4.8\">4:8</a>, <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 4:13\" href=\"/Nehemiah.4.13\">13</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 5:7\" href=\"/Nehemiah.5.7\">5:7</a>, <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 7:5\" href=\"/Nehemiah.7.5\">7:5</a>; alone, <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 2:16\" href=\"/Nehemiah.2.16\">2:16</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 12:40\" href=\"/Nehemiah.12.40\">12:40</a>; <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 13:11\" href=\"/Nehemiah.13.11\">13:11</a>; + <span dir=\"rtl\">יְהוּדִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 5:17\" href=\"/Nehemiah.5.17\">5:17</a> (v. also <a data-ref=\"Nehemiah 2:16\" href=\"/Nehemiah.2.16\">2:16</a>); + <span dir=\"rtl\">שָׂרִים</span> <a data-ref=\"Ezra 9:2\" href=\"/Ezra.9.2\">Ezr 9:2</a>. Cf. Biblical Aramaic <span dir=\"rtl\">סְגַן</span>.","next":"BDB, סָגַר","prev":"BDB, סְגֻלָּה"}